            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Suzy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this salad and it was great!. My husband and I loved it. But.....I did change a few things. First of all I did use all of the Olive Oil plus I added 3 T. of Red Wine Vinegar, garlic powder and 3T of sugar. Once I added the sugar that was La Difference! Viva! It made all the difference in the world. The dressing was so good that you could have lapped up the remaining dressing in the bottom of the bowel with some warm buttered French or Italian Bread and made a meal on that alone! Try it with the sugar. Its sensational."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dav3d"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Video for the dressing shows different ingredients than the written recipe - and it looks much better. I did a search on all recipes and found what looks to be the dressing recipe elsewhere on the site, but it makes a big batch of dressing. Here is a scaled down list of ingredients: 6 tbsp olive oil, 1 tsp garlic powder, 1 tsp dried oregano, 1 tsp dried basil, 3/4 tsp ground black pepper, 3/4 tsp salt, 3/4 tsp onion powder, 3/4 tsp Dijon-style mustard, 8 tbsp (1/2 cup) red wine vinegar.",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-17T20:22:50.307Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ADZELL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out pretty good. I made the following changes: 1) added garlic powder, an extra tsp of oregano, 1 tsp of sugar(to cut the acidity from the lemon), and 2 TBS red wine vingear to the dressing. 2) Subbed chickpeas for the olives due to personal taste. 3) Only used 1/2 of the red onion because it seemed like plenty. 4) Let my dressing sit for a few hours before adding it to the salad so the ingredients could \"get to know each other\" a little better. I appreciate how HEALTHY the salad is, and that it was very quick &amp; easy to make. Thanks for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-16T18:05:21.163Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
