              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "basg101"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad was very good. The addition of peppers to the classic Greek Salad ingredients made for an interesting twist. The dressing is a bit bland - like others I jazzed it up. I added 3 T. wine vinegar, a dash of sugar, some crushed garlic, 1 tsp. each of salt, oregano, and basil.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-23T10:19:14.070Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brushjl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great salad, can also be called Balkan salad or shepherds salad. I served tomatoes on the side (just me) and substitute banana peppers for olives but would have added olives too if I had them. Good to invest in quality feta.",
            "datePublished": "2020-08-22T22:05:50.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good and healthy, and I intend to make it all summer long. I halved the recipe and made a few small changes. Threw in 1/2 t. garlic, a chopped leaf of fresh basil, 1 t. sugar, 1 t. dijon mustard, 1/2 jar artichoke hearts, and 1 T. balsamic.",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-04T17:19:41.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Michael Minikel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Only thing I did not do was make my own dressing due to time, the salad was quick and easy to make, I used real greek olives instead of black, black olives are too bland. The olives were a bit pricey, but good friends are worth a little extra, they loved it. They never had a greek salad",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-25T22:04:28.993Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "turnmill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i added red wine vinegar to the dressing and added garlic salt turned out good next time i will soak the red onions in the dressing for a while",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-25T21:34:59.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "georgia101"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What a wonderful greek salad! A few things I've added or changed: instead of just romaine lettuce, I used an herb mix salad which consisted of a mixture of romaine lettuce, cilantro, dill, arugula lettuce, etc; I omitted the tomatoes; and I also added shredded carrots and two cucumbers instead of one. For the dressing, I didn't have a lemon so instead I used 2 limes. I also added in oregano, 3 tablespoons of rice wine vinegar and 3 tablespoons of sugar. You can add more sugar, lime juice, oregano, and/or rice vinegar to taste. Then add in some kalamata olives and sprinkle with some feta cheese! This is great, especially as a refreshing summer salad!",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-31T01:12:31.550Z"
          },
